  "node": {
    "id": "rational_curve_inner_projection_multiplicity_budget",
    "title": "Charge full inner-projection multiplicities to one genus budget",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "For a geometrically integral rational nondegenerate degree-d curve in P^r, r>=3, in characteristic0 or p>d, nonbirational inner centres satisfy sum binom(m_P+mu_P-1,2)<=binom(d-r+1,2), where m_P is the full fixed-divisor degree. In P3, d=m+mu*eta gives nu*m*binom(d-2,2)/binom(m+mu-1,2)<=(eta-1)*nu*d. Singular branch orders and infinity are retained; generic projections are counting devices, not original anchors.",
